{
 "sub_strand": "MATH.G8.GEOMET.COORDINATES_AND_GRAPHS",
 "title": "Coordinates and graphs",
 "status": "draft: written 18 Nov 2026 offline for Grade 8; not yet checked by a Kenyan maths teacher; not loaded by the live tutor",
 "sources": [],
 "notes": "Official outcomes a to h are tested; i (use IT) and j (reflect) are not questions. Coordinates are written (horizontal value, vertical value) on a Cartesian plane with all four quadrants. Drawing the axes (a) and drawing the line from a table (f) are done on graph paper; a phone question tests the labels, the steps and what a correct line looks like, and the drawing itself is for the teacher to see. Reading a fixed charge plus a rate from a fare graph is filed under reading points (b). Where a family's wrong answer is a point read just before or after the crossing, it is marked SLIP (a reading slip, not a misconception). Drawing the axes (a) and drawing the line (f) have no family yet.",
 "skills": [
  {
